EXT. HALCYON HOUSE — FRONT STEPS — NIGHT

Halcyon House at nine o'clock: a restored 1920s Black-owned hotel, every window lit. Guests climb the front steps in pairs and threes, dressed for the best night of the year. Music spills out each time the door opens.

[[TIME: 6]]
[[MUSIC: The band inside, muffled by the door; it swells each time the door opens.]]
[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[WARDROBE: GIDEON: WD-GIDEON-SUIT]]

At the top of the steps, GIDEON SHAW greets a couple by name and holds the door. Over their shoulders, something at the bottom of the steps stops him.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[ENTER: KAI]]
[[WARDROBE: KAI: WD-KAI-GE92]]

At the foot of the steps, apart from the line, KAI FONTAINE (34) waits with his hands in his pockets. Tailored waistcoat, locs braided back, lineup sharp. A man dressed for a door he knows will not open.

[[TIME: 5]]

Gideon says a quiet word to the doorman and walks down the steps. He doesn't hurry.

[[TIME: 4]]

KAI
(as Gideon reaches the bottom step)
Before you say it—

GIDEON
Not tonight, Kai.

KAI
And there it is.
(beat)
I'm not asking to come in. I know where I stand. Out here, apparently, in a very good waistcoat.

[[REACTION: GIDEON — The smallest flicker of a smile, gone at once.]]

Kai takes a folded note from inside his waistcoat and holds it out. Gideon doesn't take it. Kai doesn't lower it.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[INSERT: The folded note between them, held steady.]]

KAI
It isn't for me. That's the only reason I'm standing here.

[[HOLD: 1.5]]

Gideon takes it. Kai keeps his fingers on the note a second longer than he needs to, pressing it into Gideon's palm, then lets go.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[HANDOFF: PR-KAI-NOTE: KAI → GIDEON]]

GIDEON
Go home, Kai.

KAI
(a small, dry smile)
Working on it.

He turns and walks away down the street, past the line of arriving guests, and does not look back.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[EXIT: KAI]]

INT. HALCYON HOUSE — DOOR — NIGHT

[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[ENTER: ROYCE]]
[[WARDROBE: ROYCE: WD-ROYCE-GE92]]

The foyer: coats, laughter, the ballroom roaring beyond a pair of doors. A private staircase curves up toward the balcony. Gideon comes in from the steps with the note still in his hand.

[[TIME: 5]]

ROYCE BELL (46), somebody's plus-one and dressed to be noticed, peels away from his date at the coat check and heads straight for the staircase, two steps at a time.

[[TIME: 4]]

Gideon is simply there, on the second step, in his path. He doesn't touch him. His hands stay at his sides.

[[TIME: 3]]

ROYCE
(all charm)
Gideon Shaw. I was hoping it'd be you. Five minutes with Lockwood. She'll thank you for it.

GIDEON
There's a door for that, Royce. It isn't this one.

[[FREEZE: GIDEON SHAW: My father's right hand. My left. Has never once knocked.]]

SLOANE (V.O.)
My father's right hand. My left. Has never once knocked.

[[FREEZE: ROYCE BELL: Runs the most popular room in the city. Would like mine.]]

SLOANE (V.O.)
Runs the most popular room in the city. Would like mine.

Motion resumes. Royce laughs, genuinely delighted, and steps back down.

[[TIME: 3]]

ROYCE
Worth a try.
(lifting a glass from a passing tray)
When you get tired of standing on her stairs, mine are wider.

He goes back to his date and raises the glass to Gideon across the foyer.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[EXIT: ROYCE]]

[[SHOT: MEDIUM — SLOW PUSH]]

Alone at the foot of the staircase, Gideon looks at the note. He slips it into his inside jacket pocket, then glances up the stairs toward the balcony, where the light and the music are.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[PROP: PR-KAI-NOTE: Gideon's inside jacket pocket]]

CUT TO:
